display_code: "M"
title: How to Answer
paper: method
order: 0
---

Knowing the content is half the job. The other half is knowing how to
write an answer that earns every mark the scheme allows. This section
teaches you how to structure extended answers so you stop leaving marks
on the table.

The framework is the Answer Arc: Name, Explain, Impact. Three
components, applied in order, on every extended answer you write. The
topics here walk you through what each component does, the mistakes
students most commonly make, and worked examples showing the difference
between a weak answer, a middling one, and an answer that earns full
marks.

Read this section before you start the Paper 1 or Paper 2 content. It
gives you the framework you need to practise against while you revise.
